      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "With GetInstanceID events that require multiple sessions (because they are bigger than 80 people) could differentiate the world. Like I know one event which has 4 worlds open (named red, blue, etc in discord). Starting worlds with ID's like 10000, 20000 etc could cause the map to change dynamically to what ever ID a color is assigned and can place portals to other instances acordingly.\n\nThis way bigger events dont have to reupload the world 4 times only to change the lobby when you can just do it once, add a bit of UDON logic and change color, or whatever. Neither do people have to store 4 worlds in cache or download extra.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-09-04T20:20:20.972Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "These would be great for in-game guides and deeper integration. Imagine if enabling streamer mode could be detected by the world, and the world would switch to DMCA-friendly music? Or a map (like Among Us by Jar) having an option that required you to use the built-in avatars? What about the world being able to read Chatbox messages, allowing you to turn the chatbox into a command console, or saying a secret codeword unlocking a secret? If we could read the Instance ID, it could be used for incredibly reliable instance \nSome hypothetical nodes:\n- VRCPlayerAPI.GetAvatarID\n- VRCPlayerAPI.GetStreamMode\n- VRCPlayerAPI.GetStatus\n- VRCPlayerAPI.GetRealHeight\n- VRCPlayerAPI.GetViewpoint\n- VRCPlayerAPI.GetOnQuest\n- Event.OnPlayerAvatarChange\n- Event.OnChatboxMessageSent\n- Networking.GetInstanceID\n\nI got bored, so I opened Photoshop and made fake nodes to show what they might look like",
